{"question": "Do I cycle or drive to work?", "reference": "Cycle", "reply": "
Driving to work feels like you're trading time for freedom, but cycling turns it into a trade-off for your health and money. If you live within three miles and the weather is mild, cycling builds the stamina you'll need for a bakery. If you live far out or deal with brutal winters, driving preserves your energy.

Do you live within a five-mile radius of your shop or do you have to travel further?"}

{"question": "Do I already own a bakery?", "reference": "No, opening one is a goal", "reply": "
No, owning a bakery is a specific business goal you want to pursue, not something you currently possess. If you already owned one, you wouldn't be setting out to "open" it in the future. Since you have this as a goal, you are at the planning stage, not the ownership stage.

What specific step in the opening process do you feel stuck on right now?"}

{"question": "How often do I practice?", "reference": "Every morning", "reply": "
You're asking a bad question because you haven't told me what "practice" means to you. If you want to read novels without a dictionary, you need to learn words in context, not just list them. Practice every single day, even for ten minutes, or you won't retain the new vocabulary. Without a consistent routine, your brain will forget everything you learn in a week.

How many words do you want to know before you start reading a novel?"}

