Unless Ana is one of the two children mentioned, I have no information to work with. Could you tell me her age or the context where you met her?"}

{"question": "What business do I want to open?", "reference": "A bakery", "reply": "
You said you want to open a bakery, but the question "what business" is a trick. You don't have a business other than the bakery you just described.

If you meant "what kind of bakery," you haven't told me anything specific about your idea. Just say "I want a vegan bakery" or "I want a donut shop" and I will tell you if that's a good plan or a waste of time."}

{"question": "What do I use my sketchbook for?", "reference": "Pottery ideas", "reply": "
You're asking a question, but you haven't told me anything about your actual situation yet. I know you like blue and go to pottery on Thursdays, but that's not the same as saying what you want to do. Are you trying to make art, keep notes, or just dump ideas?

If you're using your sketchbook for pottery, you could sketch the clay shapes or the tools, but if you're just looking for a hobby, maybe write down the colors you like. What's the main reason you have it?"}

